{
    "background_story": "Ezekiel was a subway musician who had been playing his guitar in the tunnels of New York City for years. Every day, he'd set up his instrument near a busy turnstile, filling the air with soulful melodies that captivated commuters rushing to and fro. As people passed through the turnstile, they'd often pause, mesmerized by Ezekiel's talent, and toss a few coins into his guitar case. Despite the chaos of the city, Ezekiel's music brought a sense of calm and community to the bustling subway station. He became a beloved fixture, with regulars looking forward to his performances as they went about their daily routines. Ezekiel's turnstile concerts were a reminder that even in the most mundane places, beauty and joy can be found.",
